{
  "id": "artcraft",
  "name": "ArtCraft Suite (19 Creative Apps)",
  "description": "Evidence-verified agent skills for EffectCraft, FilmCraft, AniCraft, PhotoCraft, DesignCraft, and 14 more creative apps",
  "manifest_remote_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Reff33/ContextRig/main/skills_library/artcraft.json",
  "ai_instructions": "Follow the ArtCraft Creative Suite guidelines (19 open-source creative apps for motion graphics, video editing, vector, design, and 3D):\n1. Single App Focus & Zero Redundancy: Focus strictly and exclusively on the target ArtCraft app requested (e.g. `rigtools/artcraft/effectcraft/SKILL.md` for EffectCraft VFX/motion, `rigtools/artcraft/filmcraft/SKILL.md` for FilmCraft NLE video). Produce ONLY that app's native file format (`.ecproj`, `.fcproj`, etc.). NEVER generate duplicate or parallel formats (such as `.jsx`, `.html` previews, `.png` snapshots, or `.mp4` renders) in the same run unless the user explicitly asks for them.\n2. Kinetic Typography & Anti-AI-Slop Standard: When animating text or titles in EffectCraft, strictly enforce studio-grade kinetic standards from `rigtools/artcraft/effectcraft/references/kinetic-typography.md`: (a) NO raw block fade-ups; use masked horizon reveals (`overflow: hidden` / track mattes), (b) Snap-and-drift velocity curves (`cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)` / 85% easeOutExpo deceleration), (c) Word/line staggered arrivals (30–60ms), (d) Asymmetrical editorial layout (bottom-left anchors, ghost depth layers; no lazy dead-center bias), (e) Motivated fast exits (upward flick or camera push-through; never mirror the entrance), (f) Palette restraint (monochrome base + exactly one surgical accent < 5%), and (g) Clear SFX keyframe sync points.\n3. Stop & Ask Protocol (Token Guard): If the native app/CLI (`effectcraft-cli`, `filmcraft-cli`) is not installed on PATH and the user asked to execute or render, DO NOT autonomously branch out or spend tokens generating alternative renders. STOP immediately and ask the user: \"The native CLI is not installed. Would you like me to (1) scaffold the native project file only, or (2) switch to an alternative like kinet_rig to render video directly?\" Wait for user approval.\n4. Offline-First Scaffolding: When the user confirms creating project files without native apps installed, generate clean, valid native project files (`.ecproj`, `.fcproj`) without polluting the directory with extra preview files.\n5. Zero-Dependency Fallback (On User Request Only): Only use ContextRig's `kinet_rig` (Remotion) or `cut_rig` (FFmpeg) when the user explicitly approves switching to an alternative renderer.\n6. EffectCraft & After Effects: EffectCraft reads `.aep`/`.aepx` as a verified subset — never promise an After Effects-identical render; always inspect and report unsupported features.\n7. Setup & Launcher: Direct users to the ArtCraft Launcher (https://github.com/storytold/craft-launcher) or standalone CLI release zips if they wish to install native apps.",
  "claude_commands": [
    {
      "name": "artcraft",
      "content": "# /artcraft [app] [task]\n\nDrive ArtCraft creative applications (EffectCraft, FilmCraft, AniCraft, etc.) with strict single-app focus and studio-grade motion standards:\n\n1. Focus Strictly on the Target App:\n   - Produce ONLY the native file required (`.ecproj`, `.fcproj`, etc.).\n   - DO NOT spam redundant files (`.jsx`, `.html` previews, `.png` screenshots, `.mp4`) unless explicitly requested.\n2. Kinetic Typography & Anti-AI-Slop Motion Laws:\n   - Consult `rigtools/artcraft/effectcraft/references/kinetic-typography.md` when animating text in EffectCraft.\n   - Enforce: masked horizon reveals, snap-and-drift curves (`cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)`), word staggers (30-60ms), asymmetric layout (bottom-left anchors, ghost background layers), motivated fast exits, and monochrome + 1 accent color discipline.\n   - Never fade in whole text blocks simultaneously with linear or standard easing.\n3. Stop & Ask if App/CLI is Missing:\n   - If `effectcraft-cli` or `filmcraft-cli` is not installed and rendering was requested, STOP and ask the user first.\n   - Offer: (1) Scaffold native project file only, or (2) Switch to KinetRig/CutRig for immediate rendering.\n   - Do NOT spend tokens or generate alternative files without user consent.\n4. Respect App Playbooks:\n   - Consult `rigtools/artcraft/<app>/SKILL.md` for exact syntax and commands.\n   - Remember `.aep` interchange is a documented subset."
    }
  ],
  "mcp_servers": {
    "effectcraft": {
      "command": "effectcraft-cli",
      "args": [
        "mcp",
        "--autosave"
      ]
    }
  },
  "dependencies": {
    "npm": [],
    "pip": []
  },
